# Intent: find and avoid the freeze (owner report 2026-10-22, host log on 0.2.41: a turn starts, then every tool call times out for a minute with the socket still open, no reboot, no crash, memory fine). Three things in one build so the next test narrows it. (1) A stall watch in the IMU task (its own task): the application main loop bumps g_main_alive every second; if it stops for 8 s the state and free stack of the known tasks are written to flash and reported in the "boot" event as "stall" after the next restart (the host cannot be told while the loop is stuck). (2) No camera frames while the unit is not idle (listening, speaking, connecting): camera and voice together are untested hardware territory, and the freeze appeared only after the camera began to stream; the minute "camera" event counts the skipped captures as "paused". (3) The screen-flip code is compiled out (MAIPAI_SCREEN_ROTATION is not defined), so nothing can issue the panel mirror command.
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/application.cc; m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/hal_imu.cpp, hal_ws_avatar.cpp, hal_head_touch.cpp, board/stackchan.cc (MIT). Applies after 068.
# Check after a flash: if the unit freezes again, power-cycle it and read "unit boot: ... stall=main:B/... avatar_ws:B/..." in the host log: which tasks are blocked and which run; "unit camera: ... paused=N" shows captures skipped during turns. If it no longer freezes, the camera stream during turns or the screen flip was the cause.
